-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1081, found by an independent re-check: two norms on the same
-- action `x` in one state, so both untried ticks carry the label "time runs out
-- on x". Al's permission has no deadline at all, Bo's has one (a BEFORE date)
-- that the explorer cannot compute. Two different reasons, the second a real
-- gap, under one label: the coverage line names both.
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Al, Bo, Cy
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF x, c

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
h MEANS
       (PARTY Al MAY x HENCE FULFILLED)
  RAND (PARTY Bo MUST x BEFORE (YMD 2026 6 30) HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Bo)
  RAND (PARTY Cy MUST c WITHIN 3 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Cy)

#TRACE h AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Cy DOES c AT 1
